  order: 6
---

{% commandanatomy
   command="partition"
   subcommand="convert"
   input="--input concat.nex"
   inputSub="file"
   option="--output-partition raxml"
   optionSub="output format" /%}

SEGUL CLI converts single or multiple partition files between RAxML, NEXUS, and embedded NEXUS `charset` formats, including merged PartitionFinder and IQ-TREE `charpartition` schemes and strided codon models.

```bash
segul partition convert --input <a-path/wildcard-to-partition> --output-partition <output-partition-format>
```

When `-p` / `--input-partition` is omitted, SEGUL infers the input partition format from the file extension and contents.

If you output to RAxML partition and no per-partition substitution model is present, SEGUL labels DNA partitions with `--datatype dna`:

```text
DNA, locus_1 = 1-100
DNA, locus_2 = 101-150
DNA, locus_3 = 151-200
```

Merged partitions (comma- or space-separated ranges), strided ranges (`start-end\step`), and substitution models (such as `GTR+I+G` from PartitionFinder or IQ-TREE `charpartition` blocks) are preserved across RAxML and NEXUS conversions:

```text
GTR+I+G, Subset1 = 1-100\3, 201-300\3
HKY+G, Subset2 = 101-200
```

By default, `segul` checks the partition positions:

1. No duplicate partition names exist.
2. Sites cover `1..=max_end` continuously with no overlaps or gaps (including across merged and strided ranges).

Passing the `--skip-checking` flag ignores coverage and overlap checking. For example, to extract NEXUS in-file partitions (called `charset` format in `segul`):

```bash
segul partition convert --input concatenated_alignment.nex --input-partition charset --output-partition nexus
```

You can also use a wildcard to convert multiple concatenated alignment partitions at once:

```bash
segul partition convert --input ./*/concatenated_alignment.nex --input-partition charset --output-partition nexus
```

By default, SEGUL saves each converted partition next to its input file. Pass `-o` / `--output` to write converted files into a target directory instead.

## All options

| Option                     | Description                                                                                      |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `-i`, `--input`            | Partition files, or alignments with an embedded partition. Allows wildcards                      |
| `-p`, `--input-partition`  | Input partition format: `charset`, `nexus`, or `raxml` (auto-inferred when omitted)              |
| `-P`, `--output-partition` | Output partition format: `nexus` (default), `charset`, or `raxml`                                |
| `--codon`                  | Expand unstrided partitions into codon-position subsets (`\3`); existing strides are preserved   |
| `--datatype`               | Data type: `dna` (default), `aa`, or `ignore`. Sets the fallback RAxML/NEXUS label               |
| `--skip-checking`          | Skip checking partition coverage and overlaps                                                    |
| `-f`, `--input-format`     | Format of an alignment with an embedded partition: `auto` (default), `fasta`, `nexus`, or `phylip` |
| `-F`, `--output-format`    | Output sequence format: `nexus` (default), `phylip`, `fasta`, `nexus-int`, `phylip-int`, or `fasta-int` |
| `-o`, `--output`           | Output directory (defaults to each input file's directory)                                       |
| `--force`                  | Overwrite existing output files                                                                  |
| `--log`                    | Log file path. Default: `segul.log`                                                              |
